<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John George I, Prince of Anhalt-Dessau</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1567–1618</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John George I, Prince of Anhalt-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dessau">Dessau</a>, ruled the united principality of Anhalt with his brothers before its partition in 1603, when he received Dessau. He established the Calvinist principality of Anhalt-Dessau on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mulde">Mulde</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elbe">Elbe</a>, founding the line that later produced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leopold-i-prince-of-anhalt-dessau">Old Dessauer</a> and the creators of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dessau-worlitz-garden-realm">Dessau-Wörlitz Garden Realm</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-george-i-prince-of-anhalt-dessau.jpg" alt="John George I, Prince of Anhalt-Dessau" width="320" height="393" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unidentified painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:John_George_I_of_Anhalt_(cropped_from_JohannGeorgAnhDorotheaSimmern).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
